LAST_SUCCESS=Multi-child VStack wall CLEARED. Diagnosed non-invasively (wasmtime -D debug-info -D coredump, DWARF backtrace, no guest instrumentation): the "memory corruption" was actually signature_mismatch:AGGraphReadCachedAttribute — a swiftcc closure-with-arg/return ABI mismatch hit by the LAYOUT engine (Rule._cachedValue <- SizeAndSpacingContext.dynamicMember <- ViewLayoutEngine.layout) on multi-child views. NOT TupleView witness tables / NOT the unsafeBitCast existential write (both ruled out). Fixed with plain-C AGGraphReadCachedAttributeC *C variant + templatized Subgraph::cache_fetch (PlainTypeIDGetter alongside swiftcall ClosureFunctionCI) + Rule._cachedValue #if arch(wasm32) routing (heap _CachedAttrBox + @convention(c) trampoline + withoutActuallyEscaping/withExtendedLifetime). VStack{Color.red;Color.blue} -> 2 fills (red top, blue bottom, 8pt gap), exit 0, deterministic x5. VStack+@State+Text also exit 0 (@State alpha 0x40 proven; Text emits no fill = phase-4 drawer). Validated in 4s harness (cachedValue->50) then probe.
NOTES=compute-wasm.patch REGENERATED (base efb754b = HEAD harryzz/Compute wasm32-wasip1-osp, 14 files / 779 lines incl new AGGraphReadCachedAttributeC + cache_fetch templatize). probe=clean VStack{red;blue}. ALL builds ANY_ATTRIBUTE_FIX=0. NEXT: PHASE 4 = wire DisplayList -> Option-B CGContext drawer (repros/swift-canvas-spike) -> wasi:canvas -> device. Remaining bounded swiftcc walls (linker "function signature mismatch", trap only as richer views hit them, same *C fix each, validate in repros/compute-wasm/computerun first): AGGraphSearch, AGTupleWithBuffer, AGGraphWithUpdate, AGTypeApplyEnumData/MutableEnumData, AGSubgraphAddObserver, AGSubgraphApply.
